[32m+[m[32m# How to become a contributor and submit your own code[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Contributor License Agreements[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWe'd love to accept your patches! Before we can take them, we[m
[32m+[m[32mhave to jump a couple of legal hurdles.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPlease fill out either the individual or corporate Contributor License Agreement[m
[32m+[m[32m(CLA).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  * If you are an individual writing original source code and you're sure you[m
[32m+[m[32m    own the intellectual property, then you'll need to sign an[m
[32m+[m[32m    [individual CLA](https://developers.google.com/open-source/cla/individual).[m
[32m+[m[32m  * If you work for a company that wants to allow you to contribute your work,[m
[32m+[m[32m    then you'll need to sign a[m
[32m+[m[32m    [corporate CLA](https://developers.google.com/open-source/cla/corporate).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFollow either of the two links above to access the appropriate CLA and[m
[32m+[m[32minstructions for how to sign and return it. Once we receive it, we'll be able to[m
[32m+[m[32maccept your pull requests.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Contributing A Patch[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Submit an issue describing your proposed change to the[m
[32m+[m[32m   [issue tracker](https://github.com/google/googletest).[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Please don't mix more than one logical change per submittal,[m
[32m+[m[32m   because it makes the history hard to follow. If you want to make a[m
[32m+[m[32m   change that doesn't have a corresponding issue in the issue[m
[32m+[m[32m   tracker, please create one.[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Also, coordinate with team members that are listed on the issue in[m
[32m+[m[32m   question. This ensures that work isn't being duplicated and[m
[32m+[m[32m   communicating your plan early also generally leads to better[m
[32m+[m[32m   patches.[m
[32m+[m[32m1. If your proposed change is accepted, and you haven't already done so, sign a[m
[32m+[m[32m   Contributor License Agreement (see details above).[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Fork the desired repo, develop and test your code changes.[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Ensure that your code adheres to the existing style in the sample to which[m
[32m+[m[32m   you are contributing.[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Ensure that your code has an appropriate set of unit tests which all pass.[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Submit a pull request.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf you are a Googler, it is preferable to first create an internal change and[m
[32m+[m[32mhave it reviewed and submitted, and then create an upstreaming pull[m
[32m+[m[32mrequest here.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The Google Test and Google Mock Communities ##[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Google Test community exists primarily through the[m
[32m+[m[32m[discussion group](http://groups.google.com/group/googletestframework)[m
[32m+[m[32mand the GitHub repository.[m
[32m+[m[32mLikewise, the Google Mock community exists primarily through their own[m
[32m+[m[32m[discussion group](http://groups.google.com/group/googlemock).[m
[32m+[m[32mYou are definitely encouraged to contribute to the[m
[32m+[m[32mdiscussion and you can also help us to keep the effectiveness of the[m
[32m+[m[32mgroup high by following and promoting the guidelines listed here.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Please Be Friendly ###[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mShowing courtesy and respect to others is a vital part of the Google[m
[32m+[m[32mculture, and we strongly encourage everyone participating in Google[m
[32m+[m[32mTest development to join us in accepting nothing less. Of course,[m
[32m+[m[32mbeing courteous is not the same as failing to constructively disagree[m
[32m+[m[32mwith each other, but it does mean that we should be respectful of each[m
[32m+[m[32mother when enumerating the 42 technical reasons that a particular[m
[32m+[m[32mproposal may not be the best choice. There's never a reason to be[m
[32m+[m[32mantagonistic or dismissive toward anyone who is sincerely trying to[m
[32m+[m[32mcontribute to a discussion.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSure, C++ testing is serious business and all that, but it's also[m
[32m+[m[32ma lot of fun. Let's keep it that way. Let's strive to be one of the[m
[32m+[m[32mfriendliest communities in all of open source.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAs always, discuss Google Test in the official GoogleTest discussion group.[m
[32m+[m[32mYou don't have to actually submit code in order to sign up. Your participation[m
[32m+[m[32mitself is a valuable contribution.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Style[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTo keep the source consistent, readable, diffable and easy to merge,[m
[32m+[m[32mwe use a fairly rigid coding style, as defined by the [google-styleguide](https://github.com/google/styleguide) project.  All patches will be expected[m
[32m+[m[32mto conform to the style outlined [here](https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Requirements for Contributors ###[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf you plan to contribute a patch, you need to build Google Test,[m
[32m+[m[32mGoogle Mock, and their own tests from a git checkout, which has[m
[32m+[m[32mfurther requirements:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  * [Python](https://www.python.org/) v2.3 or newer (for running some of[m
[32m+[m[32m    the tests and re-generating certain source files from templates)[m
[32m+[m[32m  * [CMake](https://cmake.org/) v2.6.4 or newer[m
[32m+[m[32m  * [GNU Build System](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_Build_System)[m
[32m+[m[32m    including automake (>= 1.9), autoconf (>= 2.59), and[m
[32m+[m[32m    libtool / libtoolize.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Developing Google Test ##[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis section discusses how to make your own changes to Google Test.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Testing Google Test Itself ###[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTo make sure your changes work as intended and don't break existing[m
[32m+[m[32mfunctionality, you'll want to compile and run Google Test's own tests.[m
[32m+[m[32mFor that you can use CMake:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    mkdir mybuild[m
[32m+[m[32m    cd mybuild[m
[32m+[m[32m    cmake -Dgtest_build_tests=ON ${GTEST_DIR}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMake sure you have Python installed, as some of Google Test's tests[m
[32m+[m[32mare written in Python.  If the cmake command complains about not being[m
[32m+[m[32mable to find Python (`Could NOT find PythonInterp (missing:[m
[32m+[m[32mPYTHON_EXECUTABLE)`), try telling it explicitly where your Python[m
[32m+[m[32mexecutable can be found:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    cmake -DPYTHON_EXECUTABLE=path/to/python -Dgtest_build_tests=ON ${GTEST_DIR}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNext, you can build Google Test and all of its own tests.  On \*nix,[m
[32m+[m[32mthis is usually done by 'make'.  To run the tests, do[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    make test[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll tests should pass.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Regenerating Source Files ##[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSome of Google Test's source files are generated from templates (not[m
[32m+[m[32min the C++ sense) using a script.[m
[32m+[m[32mFor example, the[m
[32m+[m[32mfile include/gtest/internal/gtest-type-util.h.pump is used to generate[m
[32m+[m[32mgtest-type-util.h in the same directory.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mYou don't need to worry about regenerating the source files[m
[32m+[m[32munless you need to modify them.  You would then modify the[m
[32m+[m[32mcorresponding `.pump` files and run the '[pump.py](googletest/scripts/pump.py)'[m
[32m+[m[32mgenerator script.  See the [Pump Manual](googletest/docs/PumpManual.md).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Developing Google Mock ###[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis section discusses how to make your own changes to Google Mock.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### Testing Google Mock Itself ####[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTo make sure your changes work as intended and don't break existing[m
[32m+[m[32mfunctionality, you'll want to compile and run Google Test's own tests.[m
[32m+[m[32mFor that you'll need Autotools.  First, make sure you have followed[m
[32m+[m[32mthe instructions above to configure Google Mock.[m
[32m+[m[32mThen, create a build output directory and enter it.  Next,[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    ${GMOCK_DIR}/configure  # try --help for more info[m
