[32m+[m[32m# Google Test #[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m[![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/google/googletest.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/google/googletest)[m
[32m+[m[32m[![Build status](https://ci.appveyor.com/api/projects/status/4o38plt0xbo1ubc8/branch/master?svg=true)](https://ci.appveyor.com/project/GoogleTestAppVeyor/googletest/branch/master)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWelcome to **Google Test**, Google's C++ test framework![m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis repository is a merger of the formerly separate GoogleTest and[m
[32m+[m[32mGoogleMock projects. These were so closely related that it makes sense to[m
[32m+[m[32mmaintain and release them together.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPlease see the project page above for more information as well as the[m
[32m+[m[32mmailing list for questions, discussions, and development.  There is[m
[32m+[m[32malso an IRC channel on [OFTC](https://webchat.oftc.net/) (irc.oftc.net) #gtest available.  Please[m
[32m+[m[32mjoin us![m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGetting started information for **Google Test** is available in the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m[Google Test Primer](googletest/docs/Primer.md) documentation.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Google Mock** is an extension to Google Test for writing and using C++ mock[m
[32m+[m[32mclasses.  See the separate [Google Mock documentation](googlemock/README.md).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMore detailed documentation for googletest (including build instructions) are[m
[32m+[m[32min its interior [googletest/README.md](googletest/README.md) file.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Features ##[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  * An [xUnit](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XUnit) test framework.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Test discovery.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * A rich set of assertions.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * User-defined assertions.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Death tests.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Fatal and non-fatal failures.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Value-parameterized tests.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Type-parameterized tests.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Various options for running the tests.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * XML test report generation.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Platforms ##[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoogle test has been used on a variety of platforms:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Linux[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Mac OS X[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Windows[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Cygwin[m
[32m+[m[32m  * MinGW[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Windows Mobile[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Symbian[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Who Is Using Google Test? ##[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIn addition to many internal projects at Google, Google Test is also used by[m
[32m+[m[32mthe following notable projects:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  * The [Chromium projects](http://www.chromium.org/) (behind the Chrome[m
[32m+[m[32m    browser and Chrome OS).[m
[32m+[m[32m  * The [LLVM](http://llvm.org/) compiler.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * [Protocol Buffers](https://github.com/google/protobuf), Google's data[m
[32m+[m[32m    interchange format.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * The [OpenCV](http://opencv.org/) computer vision library.[m
[32m+[m[32m  * [tiny-dnn](https://github.com/tiny-dnn/tiny-dnn): header only, dependency-free deep learning framework in C++11.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Related Open Source Projects ##[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m[GTest Runner](https://github.com/nholthaus/gtest-runner) is a Qt5 based automated test-runner and Graphical User Interface with powerful features for Windows and Linux platforms.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m[Google Test UI](https://github.com/ospector/gtest-gbar) is test runner that runs[m
[32m+[m[32myour test binary, allows you to track its progress via a progress bar, and[m
[32m+[m[32mdisplays a list of test failures. Clicking on one shows failure text. Google[m
[32m+[m[32mTest UI is written in C#.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m[GTest TAP Listener](https://github.com/kinow/gtest-tap-listener) is an event[m
[32m+[m[32mlistener for Google Test that implements the[m
[32m+[m[32m[TAP protocol](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Test_Anything_Protocol) for test[m
[32m+[m[32mresult output. If your test runner understands TAP, you may find it useful.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m[gtest-parallel](https://github.com/google/gtest-parallel) is a test runner that[m
[32m+[m[32mruns tests from your binary in parallel to provide significant speed-up.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Requirements ##[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoogle Test is designed to have fairly minimal requirements to build[m
[32m+[m[32mand use with your projects, but there are some.  Currently, we support[m
[32m+[m[32mLinux, Windows, Mac OS X, and Cygwin.  We will also make our best[m
[32m+[m[32meffort to support other platforms (e.g. Solaris, AIX, and z/OS).[m
[32m+[m[32mHowever, since core members of the Google Test project have no access[m
[32m+[m[32mto these platforms, Google Test may have outstanding issues there.  If[m
[32m+[m[32myou notice any problems on your platform, please notify[m
[32m+[m[32m[googletestframework@googlegroups.com](https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/googletestframework). Patches for fixing them are[m
[32m+[m[32meven more welcome![m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Linux Requirements ###[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThese are the base requirements to build and use Google Test from a source[m
[32m+[m[32mpackage (as described below):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  * GNU-compatible Make or gmake[m
[32m+[m[32m  * POSIX-standard shell[m
[32m+[m[32m  * POSIX(-2) Regular Expressions (regex.h)[m
[32m+[m[32m  * A C++98-standard-compliant compiler[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Windows Requirements ###[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Microsoft Visual C++ 2010 or newer[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Cygwin Requirements ###[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Cygwin v1.5.25-14 or newer[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Mac OS X Requirements ###[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Mac OS X v10.4 Tiger or newer[m
[32m+[m[32m  * Xcode Developer Tools[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Contributing change[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPlease read the [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](CONTRIBUTING.md) for details on[m
[32m+[m[32mhow to contribute to this project.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mHappy testing![m
