[32m+[m[32mChanges for 1.7.0:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* All new improvements in Google Test 1.7.0.[m
[32m+[m[32m* New feature: matchers DoubleNear(), FloatNear(),[m
[32m+[m[32m  NanSensitiveDoubleNear(), NanSensitiveFloatNear(),[m
[32m+[m[32m  UnorderedElementsAre(), UnorderedElementsAreArray(), WhenSorted(),[m
[32m+[m[32m  WhenSortedBy(), IsEmpty(), and SizeIs().[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: Google Mock can now be built as a DLL.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: when compiled by a C++11 compiler, matchers AllOf()[m
[32m+[m[32m  and AnyOf() can accept an arbitrary number of matchers.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: when compiled by a C++11 compiler, matchers[m
[32m+[m[32m  ElementsAreArray() can accept an initializer list.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: when exceptions are enabled, a mock method with no[m
[32m+[m[32m  default action now throws instead crashing the test.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: added class testing::StringMatchResultListener to aid[m
[32m+[m[32m  definition of composite matchers.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: function return types used in MOCK_METHOD*() macros can[m
[32m+[m[32m  now contain unprotected commas.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement (potentially breaking): EXPECT_THAT() and ASSERT_THAT()[m
[32m+[m[32m  are now more strict in ensuring that the value type and the matcher[m
[32m+[m[32m  type are compatible, catching potential bugs in tests.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: Pointee() now works on an optional<T>.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: the ElementsAreArray() matcher can now take a vector or[m
[32m+[m[32m  iterator range as input, and makes a copy of its input elements[m
[32m+[m[32m  before the conversion to a Matcher.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: the Google Mock Generator can now generate mocks for[m
[32m+[m[32m  some class templates.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Bug fix: mock object destruction triggerred by another mock object's[m
[32m+[m[32m  destruction no longer hangs.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Improvement: Google Mock Doctor works better with newer Clang and[m
[32m+[m[32m  GCC now.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Compatibility fixes.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Bug/warning fixes.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mChanges for 1.6.0:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* Compilation is much faster and uses much less memory, especially[m
[32m+[m[32m  when the constructor and destructor of a mock class are moved out of[m
[32m+[m[32m  the class body.[m
[32m+[m[32m* New matchers: Pointwise(), Each().[m
[32m+[m[32m* New actions: ReturnPointee() and ReturnRefOfCopy().[m
[32m+[m[32m* CMake support.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Project files for Visual Studio 2010.[m
[32m+[m[32m* AllOf() and AnyOf() can handle up-to 10 arguments now.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Google Mock doctor understands Clang error messages now.[m
[32m+[m[32m* SetArgPointee<> now accepts string literals.[m
[32m+[m[32m* gmock_gen.py handles storage specifier macros and template return[m
[32m+[m[32m  types now.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Compatibility fixes.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Bug fixes and implementation clean-ups.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Potentially incompatible changes: disables the harmful 'make install'[m
[32m+[m[32m  command in autotools.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPotentially breaking changes:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* The description string for MATCHER*() changes from Python-style[m
[32m+[m[32m  interpolation to an ordinary C++ string expression.[m
[32m+[m[32m* SetArgumentPointee is deprecated in favor of SetArgPointee.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Some non-essential project files for Visual Studio 2005 are removed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mChanges for 1.5.0:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: Google Mock can be safely used in multi-threaded tests[m
[32m+[m[32m   on platforms having pthreads.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: function for printing a value of arbitrary type.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: function ExplainMatchResult() for easy definition of[m
[32m+[m[32m   composite matchers.[m
[32m+[m[32m * The new matcher API lets user-defined matchers generate custom[m
[32m+[m[32m   explanations more directly and efficiently.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Better failure messages all around.[m
[32m+[m[32m * NotNull() and IsNull() now work with smart pointers.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Field() and Property() now work when the matcher argument is a pointer[m
[32m+[m[32m   passed by reference.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Regular expression matchers on all platforms.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Added GCC 4.0 support for Google Mock Doctor.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Added gmock_all_test.cc for compiling most Google Mock tests[m
[32m+[m[32m   in a single file.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Significantly cleaned up compiler warnings.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Bug fixes, better test coverage, and implementation clean-ups.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m Potentially breaking changes:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m * Custom matchers defined using MatcherInterface or MakePolymorphicMatcher()[m
[32m+[m[32m   need to be updated after upgrading to Google Mock 1.5.0; matchers defined[m
[32m+[m[32m   using MATCHER or MATCHER_P* aren't affected.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Dropped support for 'make install'.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mChanges for 1.4.0 (we skipped 1.2.* and 1.3.* to match the version of[m
[32m+[m[32mGoogle Test):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m * Works in more environments: Symbian and minGW, Visual C++ 7.1.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Lighter weight: comes with our own implementation of TR1 tuple (no[m
[32m+[m[32m   more dependency on Boost!).[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: --gmock_catch_leaked_mocks for detecting leaked mocks.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: ACTION_TEMPLATE for defining templatized actions.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: the .After() clause for specifying expectation order.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: the .With() clause for specifying inter-argument[m
[32m+[m[32m   constraints.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: actions ReturnArg<k>(), ReturnNew<T>(...), and[m
[32m+[m[32m   DeleteArg<k>().[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: matchers Key(), Pair(), Args<...>(), AllArgs(), IsNull(),[m
[32m+[m[32m   and Contains().[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: utility class MockFunction<F>, useful for checkpoints, etc.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: functions Value(x, m) and SafeMatcherCast<T>(m).[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: copying a mock object is rejected at compile time.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: a script for fusing all Google Mock and Google Test[m
[32m+[m[32m   source files for easy deployment.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Improved the Google Mock doctor to diagnose more diseases.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Improved the Google Mock generator script.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Compatibility fixes for Mac OS X and gcc.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Bug fixes and implementation clean-ups.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mChanges for 1.1.0:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: ability to use Google Mock with any testing framework.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: macros for easily defining new matchers[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: macros for easily defining new actions.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: more container matchers.[m
[32m+[m[32m * New feature: actions for accessing function arguments and throwing[m
[32m+[m[32m   exceptions.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Improved the Google Mock doctor script for diagnosing compiler errors.[m
[32m+[m[32m * Bug fixes and implementation clean-ups.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mChanges for 1.0.0:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m * Initial Open Source release of Google Mock[m
